\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {One composite, two verdicts, and a blame walk that stops where it should.} \textbf  {(A)}~The same plan under two declared targets. Its rungs compose to $0.826\,75$ (horizontal line) in both cases; against a target of $0.70$ the step is answered and against $0.95$ it is refused. The verdict is a property of the declaration, not of the data, and the input step reports \textsf  {answer} in both runs. \textbf  {(B)}~The shortfall the diagnosis names: $0.95-0.826\,75=0.123\,25$, drawn as the part of the declared target the ladder does not reach. A refusal that named no quantity would be less useful than one that names this one. \textbf  {(C)}~The blame walk. As implemented it returns the ladder alone; had the ladder named its input as the culprit it would have returned two steps and accused a step that answered correctly. The right-hand bar is the failure mode the empty predecessor field exists to prevent, and it is checked rather than assumed. \textbf  {(D)}~The refusal surface: shortfall over composite and declared target. It is zero on and below the diagonal---where the ladder reaches its target--- and rises above it. The two markers are the two runs of panel~A, one on the flat region and one on the slope.}}{7}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:panel3}{{3}{7}{\textbf {One composite, two verdicts, and a blame walk that stops where it should.} \textbf {(A)}~The same plan under two declared targets. Its rungs compose to $0.826\,75$ (horizontal line) in both cases; against a target of $0.70$ the step is answered and against $0.95$ it is refused. The verdict is a property of the declaration, not of the data, and the input step reports \textsf {answer} in both runs. \textbf {(B)}~The shortfall the diagnosis names: $0.95-0.826\,75=0.123\,25$, drawn as the part of the declared target the ladder does not reach. A refusal that named no quantity would be less useful than one that names this one. \textbf {(C)}~The blame walk. As implemented it returns the ladder alone; had the ladder named its input as the culprit it would have returned two steps and accused a step that answered correctly. The right-hand bar is the failure mode the empty predecessor field exists to prevent, and it is checked rather than assumed. \textbf {(D)}~The refusal surface: shortfall over composite and declared target. It is zero on and below the diagonal---where the ladder reaches its target--- and rises above it. The two markers are the two runs of panel~A, one on the flat region and one on the slope}{figure.3}{}}
\newlabel{fig:panel3@cref}{{[figure][3][]3}{[1][6][]7}{}{}{}}
